1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,865
How high could you jump on other planets?

2
00:00:02,171 --> 00:00:04,430
Say you manage half a meter on Earth.

3
00:00:04,709 --> 00:00:06,853
On Mars, the same jump reaches

4
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:08,747
about 1.3 meters.

5
00:00:09,052 --> 00:00:09,971
Tiny Mercury?

6
00:00:10,276 --> 00:00:11,170
Almost the same.

7
00:00:11,462 --> 00:00:13,863
On the Moon, you'd rise 3 meters

8
00:00:13,743 --> 00:00:16,298
and float for nearly four seconds.

9
00:00:16,591 --> 00:00:19,494
On Jupiter, from a platform in its clouds,

10
00:00:19,774 --> 00:00:22,690
you'd barely clear 20 centimeters.

11
00:00:23,008 --> 00:00:25,706
Saturn has 95 times Earth's mass,

12
00:00:25,972 --> 00:00:28,270
yet you'd jump a bit higher there than at home.

13
00:00:28,562 --> 00:00:29,481
And on Pluto,

14
00:00:29,774 --> 00:00:32,265
one push sends you nearly 8 meters up.

15
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:33,515
Same legs.

16
00:00:33,794 --> 00:00:34,546
Same jump.

17
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:36,685
Gravity decides the rest.
